{"id": "EUVD-2026-93310", "enisaUuid": "151be903-b276-3325-9ce6-5cacc752016a", "description": "In the Linux kernel, the following vulnerability has been resolved:\n\nwifi: mac80211: set up the TX info early to fix failure paths\n\nThe previous commit 2c51457d930f (\"wifi: mac80211: free ack status\nframe on TX header build failure\") cleaned up the leak, but still\nleft the code a bit messy and the failed SKB didn't get reported\nto userspace.\n\nFix this up by initialising skb->cb[] earlier, which allows using\nieee80211_free_txskb() and therefore reports it for the failure\nin ieee80211_build_hdr(), and unifies the ieee80211_skb_resize()\nfailure path with it.", "datePublished": "2026-10-06T08:46:18", "dateUpdated": "2026-10-19T09:17:35", "baseScore": 0.0, "references": ["https://git.kernel.org/stable/c/df711e9fa20d7e996711c7f43a11a71805bef78d", "https://git.kernel.org/stable/c/420fcc2fdeae6ecd682d2b1605a0a54c88aed4aa", "https://git.kernel.org/stable/c/36e6f0a5e6d7238f4023e77f423c1c1414374309", "https://git.kernel.org/stable/c/0fb37d2b6cb829cebdaea80f39011469f474bdcc", "https://git.kernel.org/stable/c/03d67414bd05b86029afc14535238a9393eac1c6", "https://git.kernel.org/stable/c/50d3d79dc0743b616afb00d01a626c76758721f7"], "aliases": ["GHSA-3437-mcr8-jcvh", "CVE-2026-98325"], "assigner": "Linux", "epss": 0.18, "enisaIdProduct": [{"id": "3a9982ff-ef9a-3fea-a03d-62d3eeffd831", "product": {"name": "Linux", "vendor": {"name": "Linux"}}, "product_version": "3.6.3 <3.7"}, {"id": "3d207e56-3ee0-3630-a1b3-6131bd2bd0dd", "product": {"name": "Linux", "vendor": {"name": "Linux"}}, "product_version": "c3e7724b6bc2f25e46c38dbe68f09d71fafeafb8 <36e6f0a5e6d7238f4023e77f423c1c1414374309"}, {"id": "5022df6c-f746-3f21-a387-94e3f95596a7", "product": {"name": "Linux", "vendor": {"name": "Linux"}}, "product_version": "patch: 0"}, {"id": "6bd7b0e3-c264-32ae-8ce0-ce47aa5f89f8", "product": {"name": "Linux", "vendor": {"name": "Linux"}}, "product_version": "patch: 6.12.112"}, {"id": "882cf094